  "bio": [
    "I advance methods in AI, risk and other fields and build models of complex systems ",
    "My work spans agent-based simulation, Hepatitis C among people who inject drugs, scalable network generation, interdiction and recovery on networks, and non-probabilistic risk management.",
    "I hold an appointment in the Division of Epidemiology & Biostatistics at the University of Illinois Chicago, and roles in the tech industry. ",
    "Earlier I was adjunct professor appointment in the Department of Medicine at Loyola University Chicago, and held positions in U.S. FDA, the University of Texas at Austin and Los Alamos National Laboratory.", 
    "I received a PhD in Applied Mathematics with Computer Science from Cornell University and Master's from the University of Waterloo.",
    "My advisors were the wonderful Rick Durrett and Achim Kempf.",
    "Research with my collaborators has been supported by over $9M in grants from NIH, CDC and FDA, and has appeared in venues including Science Translational Medicine, PNAS Nexus, PLOS ONE and Scientific Reports."
  ],
